1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,601
The collision happened on a Sunday.

2
00:00:01,601 --> 00:00:10,250
Lin's mother was in the hospital ward where his grandmother had worked as a nurse, and the project meeting was at the same hour.

3
00:00:10,250 --> 00:00:14,480
“What do you expect me to say?” he asked.

4
00:00:14,480 --> 00:00:22,544
“That the study is more faithful than a family?” His sister said nothing; his brother laughed.

5
00:00:22,544 --> 00:00:30,958
The photograph on the wall — a wedding in black and white, a honeymoon in the hills — was the only picture there.

6
00:00:30,958 --> 00:00:40,522
The elder of the family, his grandfather, had been an orphan; the orphanage had given him a name and very little else.

7
00:00:40,522 --> 00:00:44,227
“A parent is a person,” he said.

8
00:00:44,227 --> 00:00:53,771
“Not an objective.” Lin felt the old fear of being superficial — an acquaintance of everyone, attached to no one.

9
00:00:53,771 --> 00:01:01,900
The word isolation pierced him more than the argument did, and something in his soul went quiet.

10
00:01:01,900 --> 00:01:05,055
His mother's voice was quiet too.

11
00:01:05,055 --> 00:01:22,158
“You have a domestic heart,” she said, “and a research heart, and only one portion of attention.” She spoke about influence, connection, attachment, and the slow transference of love from one generation to the next.

12
00:01:22,158 --> 00:01:24,803
A relative would have agreed.

13
00:01:24,803 --> 00:01:39,532
A pet rat in a junior class, a quarrel between lovers in the dormitory, a marriage that had held for thirty years: all of it belonged to the same study of how people keep promises.

14
00:01:39,532 --> 00:01:54,295
They agreed on three roles and wrote them on the back of a photograph: Lin would come home every second Sunday; Maya would host the Thursday meeting alone; the group would embrace a smaller scope until the spring.

15
00:01:54,295 --> 00:01:58,405
“This is not a separation,” Maya said.

16
00:01:58,405 --> 00:02:11,313
“It is a renegotiation, and a confidential one if you need it to be.” Confucianism, she added, had a word for it, but the plain word was enough.

17
00:02:11,313 --> 00:02:18,273
The orientation of the whole project changed by a few degrees that afternoon.

18
00:02:18,273 --> 00:02:21,553
He kept that promise five weeks.

19
00:02:21,553 --> 00:02:33,186
The book he was reading, the class he was teaching, the example of good practice set by the department: none of it mattered on the Sunday his grandfather died.

20
00:02:33,186 --> 00:02:37,351
His mother said only that she was glad he had come.

21
00:02:37,351 --> 00:02:42,295
“A voice on the telephone is not a person,” she said.

22
00:02:42,295 --> 00:02:57,024
“You know that better than your father did.” He wrote it down in the language he used for research, and then he wrote it again in his own, because the first version was the method talking and the second was him.

23
00:02:57,024 --> 00:03:09,887
Of course the group understood it: the project could not arouse the interest of a grandparent by itself, and the adoption of a smaller scope was the only honest sort of promise.

24
00:03:09,887 --> 00:03:15,562
They taught themselves to turn toward the people in the room.
